        "content": "<p>I wanted to quickly present a visualisation of Mathlib, originally created by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> for Lean 3 and recently I've updated it to Lean 4 and integrated it into <code>lake exe graph</code>:</p>\n<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/xJDEzdONrVX-5kEE1jy7IXW0/Screenshot_20240902_141149.png\">Screenshot_20240902_141149.png</a><br>\n<a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/gMuahKYDKk3wXJbR2PWca4cV/Screenshot_20240910_102417.png\">Screenshot_20240910_102417.png</a></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/xJDEzdONrVX-5kEE1jy7IXW0/Screenshot_20240902_141149.png\" title=\"Screenshot_20240902_141149.png\"><img data-original-dimensions=\"2880x1544\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/xJDEzdONrVX-5kEE1jy7IXW0/Screenshot_20240902_141149.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/gMuahKYDKk3wXJbR2PWca4cV/Screenshot_20240910_102417.png\" title=\"Screenshot_20240910_102417.png\"><img data-original-dimensions=\"2177x1552\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/gMuahKYDKk3wXJbR2PWca4cV/Screenshot_20240910_102417.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><p>You can explore the graph yourself at <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/mathlib.html\">https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/mathlib.html</a><br>\nHovering over a node highlight the part of mathlib which are depening on that node:</p>\n<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/VJDTRjzcXTUUA7ngdqmStcDq/Screenshot_20240910_101803.png\">Screenshot_20240910_101803.png</a></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/VJDTRjzcXTUUA7ngdqmStcDq/Screenshot_20240910_101803.png\" title=\"Screenshot_20240910_101803.png\"><img data-original-dimensions=\"2170x1543\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/VJDTRjzcXTUUA7ngdqmStcDq/Screenshot_20240910_101803.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><p>The graph is automatically updated (together with the mathlib docs) and is currently only linked from the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib_stats.html\">mathlib stats page</a>.</p>\n<p>You can create these kind of interactive graphs for your own project, by depending on <code>mathlib</code> or more precisely on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/import-graph\"><code>importGraph</code></a>. Then the usual <code>lake exe graph</code> command with a <code>.html</code> output file should produce a stand-alone HTML file.</p>\n<p>For example, here is a subgraph of mathlib going to <code>Probability.Kernel.CondDistrib</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>lake<span class=\"w\"> </span>exe<span class=\"w\"> </span>graph<span class=\"w\"> </span>--to<span class=\"w\"> </span>Mathlib.Probability.Kernel.CondDistrib<span class=\"w\"> </span>example.html\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/e8UjJPNVZNXc1WS2Sh08Fksd/Screenshot_20240910_102114.png\">Screenshot_20240910_102114.png</a></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/e8UjJPNVZNXc1WS2Sh08Fksd/Screenshot_20240910_102114.png\" title=\"Screenshot_20240910_102114.png\"><img data-original-dimensions=\"2170x1543\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/e8UjJPNVZNXc1WS2Sh08Fksd/Screenshot_20240910_102114.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/MYTHc7eoQCHbeuzu54X9loB4/example.html\">example.html</a></p>",
